body:grpc {
  name: message 1
  content: '''
    {
      "digest": "REPLACE_WITH_A_TRANSACTION_DIGEST",
      "read_mask": {
        "paths": ["digest", "checkpoint", "transaction.sender", "effects"]
      }
    }
  '''
}

docs {
  Fetch a single transaction by digest.

  **Service:** `sui.rpc.v2.LedgerService` · **Method:** `GetTransaction` (unary)

  **Request fields:**
  - `digest` (required string): the transaction digest.
  - `read_mask` (optional FieldMask): fields to populate. Defaults to
    `digest` if omitted.

  Replace `digest` with a real transaction digest — e.g. pull one from
  `GetCheckpoint`'s `transactions` field, or from a block explorer.

  **Caveat found while testing:** requesting the `checkpoint` field mask on
  a synthetic per-checkpoint system transaction (e.g. a
  `ConsensusCommitPrologue`, identifiable by `sender = 0x0…0`) returned
  `NOT_FOUND`, even though the same digest resolves fine with a narrower
  mask (e.g. `digest` only) or via `BatchGetTransactions`. Regular
  user-submitted transactions were unaffected. Worth confirming with
  Mysten/node operators if you hit unexpected `NOT_FOUND`s.

  Verified against `sui-mainnet.g.alchemy.com` with a real transaction digest.
}
